<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Fyffes buys rest of Sunpak &amp; Mayfield.</title>
<headline>Fyffes buys rest of Sunpak &amp; Mayfield.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's fresh fruit distributor Fyffes Plc said on Monday that it has agreed to acquire the remaining 49.9 percent of shares it does not already own in Sunpak and Mayfield Fresh Produce Ltd, the Cork-based fresh fruit and produce company.</p>
<p>The consideration payable on completion is 1.575 million Irish pounds and the issue of 1.375 million new ordinary shares in Fyffes. An additional 750,000 pounds may also be payable, the company said.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom 353-1-661-3377</p>
</text>
